# 16. NCD Management Module

NCD management should be a configurable program layer.

Initial diseases:

```text
NCD PROGRAM
│
├── Diabetes
├── Cardiac / Cardiovascular
└── Sickle Cell
```

The system must allow:

```text
+ Add New NCD Disease
```

Examples of future additions:

* Hypertension
* Chronic Kidney Disease
* Cancer
* Other NCD programs

No major system redesign should be required to add a new disease.

---

# 17. NCD Disease Configuration

Each disease can have its own configuration.

```text
NCD Disease
    ↓
NCD Protocol
    ↓
Screening Configuration
    ↓
Risk Factors
    ↓
Clinical Criteria
    ↓
Required Services
    ↓
Follow-up Schedule
    ↓
CRFs / Assessments
```

A disease configuration may define:

* Screening questions
* Risk factors
* Symptoms
* Measurements
* Required laboratory tests
* ECG requirements
* Echo requirements
* Imaging requirements
* Diagnostic criteria
* Follow-up rules
* Outcome definitions
* Required forms

The exact clinical criteria should be controlled by the approved clinical protocol.

---

# 18. NCD Screening

A patient can be screened for one or more NCDs.

Example:

```text
Patient
   │
   └── NCD Screening
        │
        ├── Diabetes       ✓
        ├── Cardiac        ✓
        └── Sickle Cell   Not selected
```

The system should not force every patient through every disease screening pathway.

---

# 19. Screening and Diagnostic Work-up

Screening may require clinical services.

For example:

```text
NCD Screening
      ↓
Risk Assessment
      ↓
Clinical Assessment
      ↓
Laboratory
      ↓
ECG / Echo / Imaging where required
      ↓
Assessment
      ↓
Screening / Diagnostic Result
```

The same clinical services are reused elsewhere in the system.

