# 48. Visit Definition

Each visit definition may contain:

```text
VisitDefinition
│
├── Visit Name
├── Visit Code
├── Sequence
├── Relative Timing
├── Required CRFs
├── Required Clinical Services
├── Required Assessments
├── Required Laboratory
├── Required Diagnostics
└── Required Procedures
```

---

# 49. Patient-Specific Schedule

The actual patient's schedule should be generated from the plan but stored independently.

This is important because staff may modify the patient's future schedule.

```text
Protocol / NCD Plan
        ↓
Schedule Rule
        ↓
Patient Schedule
        ↓
Patient Visits
```

Changing the master configuration should not blindly rewrite historical patient schedules.

---

# 50. Follow-up Example — Diabetes

Configuration:

```text
Disease: Diabetes
Scheduling Mode: Automatic
Frequency: Every 3 months
Reference: Baseline
Generate ahead: 12 months
Maximum future visits: 4
```

Patient:

```text
Baseline: September 2026

Upcoming:
December 2026
March 2027
June 2027
September 2027
```

At December:

```text
December → Completed
```

The system generates:

```text
December → Completed
March     → Planned
June      → Planned
September → Planned
December  → Newly generated
```

---

# 51. Follow-up Example — Cardiac

Configuration:

```text
Frequency: Every 1 month
Generate ahead: 3 months
Maximum future visits: 3
```

The system maintains three upcoming visits.

If the clinician changes the patient to every three months, the future schedule can be recalculated while preserving completed history.

---

# 52. Follow-up Example — Research Study

A research protocol may specify:

```text
Baseline
Day 7
Day 14
Day 30
Day 90
Day 180
Day 365
```

This can be configured as a custom schedule rather than forcing a monthly frequency.

---

# 53. Outcome Management

Outcome should be treated as a separate lifecycle/status concept.

Possible statuses include:

```text
Ongoing
Completed
Lost to Follow-up
Death
Transfer Out
Withdrawal
```

The exact terminology can be configured per study/program.

When an outcome terminates follow-up, future visits may automatically become:

```text
Not Applicable / Cancelled
```

with an audit trail.

