# 57. Automatic Scheduling Algorithm

Conceptually:

```text
1. Identify active follow-up plan
2. Identify patient's reference date
3. Identify existing future planned visits
4. Calculate generation window
5. Calculate maximum allowed future visits
6. Generate missing visits
7. Do not duplicate existing visits
8. Do not modify completed visits
9. Apply current active scheduling rules
10. Record audit information
```

Example:

```text
Maximum future visits = 3

Existing:
Nov
Dec
Jan

Completed:
Oct
```

No new visit is generated because three future visits already exist.

After November is completed:

```text
Dec
Jan
Feb ← generated
```

