# 60. Patient vs Research Data

The system should maintain a shared patient identity while protecting study-specific information.

```text
Patient
   │
   ├── Hospital Care
   │
   ├── NCD Program
   │
   └── Research Study
```

Research users should only see study information according to their permissions.

Organizational and disease-level access must also apply to research data.

For example:

* A study coordinator may access participants at assigned facilities.
* A national research coordinator may access authorized study data across the country.
* A disease program coordinator may access disease-specific NCD data but not unrelated study data.
* A monitor may access only assigned studies and sites.

