# 66. Important Scheduling Rules

The system should enforce these principles:

### Rule 1

A future planned visit can be changed according to permissions.

### Rule 2

A future planned visit with no data can be deleted if permitted.

### Rule 3

Completed visits should not normally be deleted.

### Rule 4

Historical clinical/research data must remain auditable.

### Rule 5

Changing frequency should affect future scheduling, not rewrite history.

### Rule 6

Unscheduled encounters can occur at any time.

### Rule 7

An unscheduled encounter should not automatically replace a scheduled study visit.

### Rule 8

Automatic scheduling must avoid duplicate visits.

### Rule 9

Maximum future visits must be respected.

### Rule 10

Generation horizon must be respected.

### Rule 11

Baseline, last completed visit, and custom date/month must be supported as reference points.

### Rule 12

Users may only view or modify schedules within their assigned facility, organizational level, disease, program, or study scope.

### Rule 13

National coordinators may access country-wide data only when their role and permissions authorize it.

### Rule 14

Disease-level access must be enforced independently from organizational-level access.

