# 68. Final Functional Principle

The system should be built around the following model:

```text
PATIENT
   ↓
CONTEXT
   ├── Hospital Care
   ├── NCD Program
   └── Research Study
          ↓
       ENCOUNTER / STUDY VISIT
          ↓
       CLINICAL ACTIVITIES
          ├── Triage
          ├── Consultation
          ├── Laboratory
          ├── ECG
          ├── Echo
          ├── Radiology
          ├── Pharmacy
          └── Other Services
          ↓
       FOLLOW-UP PLAN
          ↓
       SCHEDULED VISITS
          │
          ├── Automatic
          ├── Manual
          └── Hybrid
          │
          ├── Frequency
          ├── Reference Point
          ├── Generate Ahead
          └── Maximum Future Visits
          ↓
       OUTCOMES
```

The central architectural rule is:

> **Clinical services are reusable, while NCD programs and research protocols define how those services are used.**

The access-control rule is:

> **Users access data according to their role, facility or organizational level, disease or program assignment, study assignment, and approved permissions.**

This allows the same platform to support today's **Diabetes, Cardiac, and Sickle Cell programs**, future NCDs, general hospital care, and clinical research without rebuilding the underlying system, while enabling authorized users and national coordinators to work effectively at facility, district, regional, zonal, country, and disease-specific levels.
